WEBVTT

00:00.821 --> 00:03.233
Estimate stuck before
it reaches the customer?

00:03.338 --> 00:05.971
Nepsis maps, improves, tests,

00:06.026 --> 00:08.489
and hands over one
recurring workflow.

00:08.544 --> 00:10.821
Follow this estimate
from request to sent.

00:12.469 --> 00:15.449
A homeowner asks for an estimate
on a residential addition.

00:15.504 --> 00:17.284
The request becomes site notes,

00:17.339 --> 00:20.270
measurements, photographs, office intake,

00:20.325 --> 00:22.447
pricing, a formatted estimate,

00:22.502 --> 00:24.978
and finally an email
to the customer.

00:25.147 --> 00:27.085
That sounds like one straight line.

00:27.185 --> 00:29.391
In practice, several
people touch it,

00:29.446 --> 00:31.226
and every handoff can add a wait

00:31.281 --> 00:32.633
or send it backward.

00:35.816 --> 00:38.976
Nepsis starts by mapping the
route as it actually runs.

00:39.102 --> 00:40.967
The enquiry reaches the site visit.

00:41.022 --> 00:42.918
The site notes reach the office.

00:42.973 --> 00:45.779
The office checks whether the
pack is ready for pricing.

00:45.834 --> 00:47.969
The owner applies pricing judgment.

00:48.095 --> 00:50.728
The office prepares the
customer-facing estimate.

00:50.783 --> 00:52.136
Nothing is simplified yet,

00:52.191 --> 00:53.801
and no tool is chosen.

00:53.871 --> 00:56.447
The first job is to make
the current route visible.

00:59.687 --> 01:01.694
Now watch where the estimate stops.

01:01.805 --> 01:03.472
The owner’s tray is not just full

01:03.527 --> 01:04.581
of pricing work.

01:04.636 --> 01:07.380
One pack has measurements
but no photographs.

01:07.476 --> 01:09.426
Another has a scope
question with no

01:09.481 --> 01:11.048
named person to answer it.

01:11.103 --> 01:13.856
A third looks complete
until pricing begins.

01:13.991 --> 01:16.466
The owner is receiving
work that is nearly ready,

01:16.521 --> 01:19.027
then spending attention
chasing what is missing.

01:19.172 --> 01:21.091
The hold is the
readiness handoff into

01:21.146 --> 01:21.873
pricing.

01:25.654 --> 01:28.432
That does not mean the whole
business needs rebuilding.

01:28.601 --> 01:30.679
Nepsis and the owner
agree a boundary

01:30.734 --> 01:33.197
around one segment: ready to price,

01:33.252 --> 01:35.031
priced, and ready to send.

01:35.086 --> 01:36.655
Site visits stay outside.

01:36.856 --> 01:38.891
Pricing judgment
stays with the owner.

01:38.946 --> 01:41.188
Unrelated systems stay outside.

01:41.378 --> 01:43.769
The boundary says
exactly what can change,

01:43.853 --> 01:45.675
what cannot, and what the team will

01:45.730 --> 01:46.358
test.

01:49.626 --> 01:51.961
Inside that boundary,
the rule comes before

01:52.016 --> 01:53.071
the software.

01:53.143 --> 01:55.520
A ready-to-price pack
has the agreed notes,

01:55.575 --> 01:58.762
measurements, photographs,
and scope questions in one

01:58.817 --> 01:59.587
place.

01:59.756 --> 02:02.480
A named office check
confirms the pack is ready.

02:02.547 --> 02:05.274
Missing information follows
an exception route instead

02:05.329 --> 02:07.407
of entering the
owner’s pricing tray.

02:07.462 --> 02:09.956
Ownership is visible at every step.

02:10.011 --> 02:12.221
Existing tools can
support that method where

02:12.276 --> 02:14.397
they fit; a different
tool is considered

02:14.452 --> 02:16.345
only if the workflow needs it.

02:20.100 --> 02:22.640
Then the people who will
use it run the process.

02:22.830 --> 02:26.053
First, the team moves a normal
estimate through the route.

02:26.108 --> 02:29.033
Next, they test a
changed-scope case.

02:29.138 --> 02:31.891
Then a pack arrives without
a required photograph.

02:31.954 --> 02:33.648
If an instruction is unclear,

02:33.703 --> 02:36.720
the team changes the instruction
and runs the case again.

02:36.775 --> 02:38.784
The goal is not a
good-looking demo.

02:38.839 --> 02:42.894
It is a workflow the team can operate,
including an ordinary exception.

02:46.606 --> 02:48.898
Handoff means the team
receives the operating

02:48.953 --> 02:50.434
note, the named owner,

02:50.489 --> 02:52.666
the normal route, and the fallback.

02:52.793 --> 02:55.317
The consultant stops
directing every move.

02:55.448 --> 02:57.313
The office runs the next estimate,

02:57.368 --> 03:01.774
the owner keeps the pricing decision, and
the exception has somewhere clear to go.

03:05.005 --> 03:06.650
That is what Nepsis does:

03:06.712 --> 03:08.975
map the work, find the hold,

03:09.101 --> 03:10.667
agree a bounded improvement,

03:10.722 --> 03:12.332
configure it, test it,

03:12.387 --> 03:13.796
and hand it over.

03:13.965 --> 03:15.916
Bring one recurring
workflow to a free

03:15.971 --> 03:17.068
consultation.

03:17.224 --> 03:19.857
You receive a concise
Basic Diagnosis,

03:19.912 --> 03:21.793
then decide whether to continue.
